+#    ($vwatch) that runs gate.py and polls the chain (pid + start time, every VM_GATE_WATCH s, 1); when the chain is gone
+#    (its scope stopped by stop-at-boundary.sh / freeze-mover.sh, a manual stop or kill) it stops its own scope ($vunit:
+#    the gate and everything in it), then TERMs (KILL after VM_GATE_STOP_GRACE s, 30) the gate's tree if anything is left.
+#    The slot is kept until that scope is gone: the watcher records its scope (cgroup, else its own pid + start time) in
